I am excited to apply for your Software Developer role. Having taught both Computer Science and Mathematics for nine years, I have seen first-hand how impactful the support of organisations like Raspberry Pi can be. Over the past three years, my passion for improving the teaching of Computer Science has only deepened, and I am eager to take on a role that allows me to support and inspire both students and teachers on a much wider scale. 

I have mentored teachers who are new to teaching both Mathematics and Computer Science and collaborated across departments to redesign Electrical and Electronic Engineering modules to meet shifting specifications. Key to this was listening to the needs of colleagues and respond with practical, supportive solutions. I aim to foster a collaborative environment and support the professional growth of others in any setting I find myself in.

I have always sought out additional opportunities to use my skills to create, evaluate and improve various resources for students to work on. This ranges from research-driven PRIMM worksheets to procedural question generation for Dr Frost Maths. Building on my experience with Dr Frost Maths, I have begin building my own platform for question generation, testing and revising for use within my own department. I wish to keep using my passion for computing in the wider world and hope to use my pedagogical expertise and subject knowledge continue developing high-quality resources for teachers and students alike.

I am enthusiastic about engaging students beyond the classroom, allowing them to see their skills solve problems, engage with industry partners, and build the soft skills vital to their futures. I have led student engineering teams to a variety of national competitions and am currently collaborating with colleagues to develop an outreach program aimed at addressing gender disparities within STEM. By actively working to widen participation and ensuring that all learners see themselves represented in the curriculum, I hope to take every chance to help Raspberry Pi continue to remove barriers to success for students from all backgrounds.

Having balanced nine years of teaching with a variety of other roles, I have developed both the technical rigor and pedagogical insight necessary to thrive in this position. This foundation, combined with my drive to improve my skils and to help students engage with computing in a meaningful way, ensures I am well-prepared to contribute to the Raspberry Pi Foundation's mission of enhancing educational standards and accessibility. I am eager to bring this same level of enthusiasm to the Software Development team and welcome the opportunity to discuss my application further. Please do not hesitate to reach out should you have any questions or require additional details regarding my background.

Sincerely,\ 
